4. Library source when giving others access

When you distribute the Library, or distribute a program containing or using it,
you must concurrently make the corresponding Library source publicly accessible
without charge and give recipients a clear link or access instructions.

When you provide other people with an online service that uses the Library,
you must make the corresponding Library source publicly accessible without
charge while that service is available, with a clear source link or access
instructions in the service or its documentation.

The required source is the Library version actually used, including all your
modifications to it and the files needed to build those modifications. Source
must be in its preferred editable form. An unmodified Library may be provided
by linking to an accessible upstream archive or commit for that exact version.
If you modified it, an upstream link alone is insufficient: provide your
modified Library source or the exact upstream version together with complete
modification patches and build instructions.

This obligation covers the Library and changes to it, not the entire application,
unrelated application code, business data, logs, secrets, or separately licensed
third-party dependencies. Retain the copyright and license notices with the
published Library source. Source publication does not make Commercial Use free.

